$DIR/test.p:3:19: cannot use "x" (constant of type string) as error value in return statement: string does not implement error (missing method Error)
    A value can be used as an interface only if its type has every method the
    interface lists, with the same parameters and results. Types satisfy
    interfaces without saying so, so a missing method shows up where the value
    is used.
    The message names the missing or mismatched method. A method declared on *T
    belongs to *T, not to T, so you may need to use a pointer.
    (see "Interface types" in the Plutonium spec, section 7.9)
    (run "pluto explain E0021" for a longer explanation)
